{number: 69}
{title: ‘Tis So Sweet to Trust in Jesus}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] 'Tis so sweet to trust in Jesus,
Just to take Him at His [G7] word;
[C] Just to rest upon His promise,
Just to [G7] know, "Thus saith the [C] Lord."
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] Jesus, Jesus, how I trust Him!
How I've proved Him o'er and [G7] o'er!
[C] Jesus, Jesus, precious Jesus!
O for [G7] grace to trust Him [C] more!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
O how [C] sweet to trust in Jesus,
Just to trust His cleansing [G7] blood;
[C] Just in simple faith to plunge me
'Neath the [G7] healing, cleansing [C] flood!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Yes, 'tis [C] sweet to trust in Jesus,
Just from sin and self to [G7] cease;
[C] Just from Jesus simply taking
Life and [G7] rest, and joy and [C] peace.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
I'm so [C] glad I learned to trust Thee,
Precious Jesus, Savior, [G7] Friend;
And I [C] know that Thou art with me,
Wilt be [G7] with me to the [C] end.
{end_of_verse}
